### Upgrading a Consul cluster deployed by an older JHipster version

The Consul servers encrypt their gossip traffic with the key of the `consul-gossip-key` Secret, and servers deployed by an older JHipster version can't talk to them: a rolling update stalls on its first pod. Replace the cluster instead of running `helm-upgrade.sh` alone. This deletes the data of the Consul servers, so restart `consul-config-loader`, wait until your configuration is in Consul, then restart your apps to register them again:

```
kubectl delete statefulset consul<%- namespaceOption %>
kubectl get pvc -o name<%- namespaceOption %> | grep -E '^persistentvolumeclaim/data-consul-[0-9]+$' | xargs -r kubectl delete<%- namespaceOption %>
bash helm-upgrade.sh
kubectl rollout status statefulset/consul<%- namespaceOption %>
kubectl rollout restart deployment/consul-config-loader<%- namespaceOption %>
kubectl rollout status deployment/consul-config-loader<%- namespaceOption %>
until kubectl exec consul-0<%- namespaceOption %> -- consul kv get config/application/data > /dev/null 2>&1; do sleep 2; done
  <%_ if (consulApps.length > 0) { _%>
kubectl rollout restart <%- consulApps.map(app => `deployment/${app}`).join(' ') %><%- namespaceOption %>
  <%_ } _%>
```

`helm-upgrade.sh` recreates the StatefulSet and removes the old `gossip-key` Secret of the `csvc` chart.

